'''''Sedum rubens''''' is a species of annual herb in the family [[Crassulaceae]]. They are succulent plants. They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 5.4&nbsp;cm.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Sedum rubens L. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/5545923|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org|archive-date=2022-03-07|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220307194601/https://eol.org/pages/5545923|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Sedum rubens (Red Stonecrop) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/CRSS/Sedum_rubens.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us |archive-date=2021-12-27 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211227185600/https://www.maltawildplants.com/CRSS/Sedum_rubens.php |url-status=live }}</ref>

